                  </origin>
                  <provenance type="#m"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_420">Oxford, Oxfordshire.
                        Franciscan convent</orgName><p>The manuscript contains marginalia similar
                        to those in BL MS Harley 3249, and Cambridge, Corpus Christi College, MS 135
                        (ex inform. David Rundle). The manuscript also contains the best witness to
                        Robert Grosseteste's translation of John of Damascus, leading to the surmise
                        that it was probably made by and belonged to the Oxford Franciscans, to whom
                        Grosseteste left his books. (See further M. Holland, 'Robert Grosseteste's
                        translation of John of Damascus's The Dialogue of the Christian and the
                        Saracen', in Robert Grosseteste and His Intellectual Milieu, ed. J. Flood
                        &amp; others (Toronto 2013), 248--93, at p. 253.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Given to Magdalen College at the end of s.
                     xv: 'Codex collegii beate marie magdalenes in oxonia Ex donon Magistri Ioannis
                     Sydnere quondam socii eiusdem collegii' (fol. 9v). John Sydner was a fellow of
                     the college c. 1475 and the donor of three other books in the library (BRUO
                     1839). Normal 0 false false false EN-GB X-NONE X-NONE </provenance>
               </history>
